  "term": "sexual assault",
  "definition": "Sexual assault is any attempt to obtain sexual acts through coercion or force, including rape by an intimate partner or a stranger. In psychology, it is recognized as a traumatic experience that can be associated with post-traumatic stress reactions such as hyperarousal, numbness, dissociation, and other lasting difficulties.",
